Traffic Priority marks chosen connections with a DSCP: classes by
interface, address, port and the DSCP a connection arrives with, each
written as one pf match rule per interface, IP version and address
pair, registered by the plugin at every filter reload and never added
to the owner's own rules. pf writes the class's DSCP into every packet
of its connections, both ways, the ECN bits kept. On a
Sophos XGS, os-xgs-npu gives an IPv4 connection in hardware the DSCP pf
marked it with (measured there with a normalization rule; with these
rules not yet). Firewall: Shaper is neither read nor written, and no
switch queue is set: that mapping is not measured yet.

